lated.", "Incumbent Kathy Castor (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Kathy Castor, a Democratic incumbent seeking another term, faces Republican nominee Mike Beltran in a redrawn Tampa-area district that now leans slightly Republican. Castor has raised about $2.3 million and holds a cash advantage, while Democratic-aligned groups have spent heavily attacking Beltran's ties to Trump's policies. Beltran has also raised over $2 million and has campaigned aggressively, casting Castor as out of touch.\n\nIndependent raters are split, with several calling the race a Tossup and others leaning Democratic, and prediction markets give Castor roughly a two-in-three chance. The only available poll, from July, showed Castor ahead by eight points, but it is dated. National Democrats have scheduled appearances in the district, signaling both sides see it as competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7914, "margin": 4.84}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7727, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.766, "margin": 4.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7799, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7024, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6958, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7726, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7812, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.75, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7285, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7934, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7587, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7793, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7357, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7597, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.738, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7638, "margin": 4.5}]}